---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";

const updated = "July 10, 2026";
---
<Base
  title="backlex — Privacy Policy"
  description="How backlex collects, uses, stores, and protects your personal data."
>
  <section class="relative z-[1] max-w-[760px] mx-auto px-8 max-md:px-5 py-20">
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-3 mb-12">
      <span class="inline-block self-start font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-muted-foreground border border-border rounded-full px-3 py-1.5 bg-muted">
        Legal
      </span>
      <h1 class="font-display font-light text-[clamp(32px,5vw,48px)] -tracking-[0.03em] leading-[1.05]">
        Privacy Policy
      </h1>
      <p class="text-[13px] text-muted-foreground">Last updated: {updated}</p>
    </div>

    <div class="flex flex-col gap-8 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
      <p>
        This Privacy Policy explains how backlex ("the Service", "we") collects,
        uses, stores, and protects your personal data when you use the
        backlex.com website or the backlex managed cloud. It is our transparency
        notice under Article 13 of the GDPR and Article 10 of the KVKK. We
        process most of your data to perform our contract with you and to meet
        legal obligations; where we rely on your consent, we ask for it
        separately and you may withdraw it at any time.
      </p>

      <p>
        The data controller is Furkan Kinyas, an individual established in
        Türkiye, operating as backlex, reachable at
        <a href="mailto:hi@backlex.com" class="text-foreground underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-primary transition-colors">hi@backlex.com</a>.
        Our postal address is available on request.
      </p>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-[19px] font-semibold text-foreground -tracking-[0.02em] mb-3">1. Information We Collect</h2>
        <p class="mb-3">To provide the Service we collect:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 flex flex-col gap-2">
          <li><strong class="text-foreground font-medium">Account information</strong> — the name, email address, and password you provide at sign-up. Passwords are stored only as a one-way hash, never in plain text.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-foreground font-medium">Organization &amp; project data</strong> — the organizations, projects, and billing configuration you create.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-foreground font-medium">Session &amp; authentication data</strong> — session tokens issued at sign-in and security-related logs.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-foreground font-medium">Usage data</strong> — technical records of how you interact with the Service (IP address, browser type, access times).</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-[19px] font-semibold text-foreground -tracking-[0.02em] mb-3">2. How We Use Information</h2>
        <p class="mb-3">We use the information we collect only to:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 flex flex-col gap-2 mb-3">
          <li>Create your account, authenticate you, and manage your session.</li>
          <li>Provide, maintain, and improve the Service.</li>
          <li>Process billing and payments.</li>
          <li>Keep the Service secure and prevent unauthorized access.</li>
          <li>Communicate with you about important service matters.</li>
          <li>Meet our legal obligations.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mb-3">Our legal bases for this processing (GDPR Article 6; KVKK Article 5) are:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 flex flex-col gap-2">
          <li><strong class="text-foreground font-medium">Performance of our contract with you</strong> — to create and run your account, provide the Service, and process billing.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-foreground font-medium">Our legitimate interests</strong> — to keep the Service secure, prevent abuse, and improve it.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-foreground font-medium">Legal obligation</strong> — to meet tax, accounting, and other statutory duties.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-foreground font-medium">Your consent</strong> — where we ask for it separately; you can withdraw it at any time.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-[19px] font-semibold text-foreground -tracking-[0.02em] mb-3">3. Sharing of Information</h2>
        <p class="mb-3">We do not sell your personal data. We share it only:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 flex flex-col gap-2 mb-3">
          <li>With service providers (sub-processors) who help us operate the Service and process data on our behalf and under our instructions.</li>
          <li>When required by a legal obligation or a valid official request.</li>
          <li>With your explicit consent.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mb-3">Our current sub-processors are:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 flex flex-col gap-2">
          <li><strong class="text-foreground font-medium">Cloudflare</strong> — cloud infrastructure, compute, and storage.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-foreground font-medium">Polar Software Inc.</strong> — payments, as our Merchant of Record.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-foreground font-medium">Resend</strong> — transactional email delivery.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-3">
          We will update this list before adding or replacing a sub-processor.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-[19px] font-semibold text-foreground -tracking-[0.02em] mb-3">4. Data Security</h2>
        <p>
          We apply reasonable technical and organizational measures — such as
          encryption, access control, and secure authentication — to protect
          your data against unauthorized access, alteration, and loss. No method
          of transmission or storage is 100% secure.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-[19px] font-semibold text-foreground -tracking-[0.02em] mb-3">5. Data Retention</h2>
        <p>
          We keep your personal data only while your account is active or as long
          as needed to fulfil the purposes described in this policy. We do not
          delete your data when a paid plan ends — your organization reverts to
          the Free plan. Your project database stays available for export for at
          least 30 days after a plan ends or an account is closed, after which we
          may permanently delete it. When you delete your account, your data is
          removed within a reasonable period, subject to any legal retention
          obligations.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-[19px] font-semibold text-foreground -tracking-[0.02em] mb-3">6. Data Residency</h2>
        <p class="mb-3">
          When you create an organization you choose where your project database
          is stored: the European Union or Global. That choice determines the
          database's location. It does not confine everything else — compute runs
          on a global edge network, and files you upload to storage are held on
          our infrastructure provider's global network, wherever your database
          sits.
        </p>
        <p>
          backlex is operated from Türkiye, so your data may be accessed by us
          from there. Türkiye is not covered by a European Commission adequacy
          decision. If you are in the EU/EEA and need a specific transfer
          safeguard for your organization, contact us at
          <a href="mailto:hi@backlex.com" class="text-foreground underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-primary transition-colors">hi@backlex.com</a>.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-[19px] font-semibold text-foreground -tracking-[0.02em] mb-3">7. Cookies &amp; Sessions</h2>
        <p>
          We use strictly necessary cookies and similar technologies to keep you
          signed in and to authenticate you. These are essential to the core
          operation of the Service; blocking them in your browser may prevent
          parts of the Service from working correctly.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-[19px] font-semibold text-foreground -tracking-[0.02em] mb-3">8. Your Rights</h2>
        <p class="mb-3">
          Under applicable law (the GDPR and the KVKK) you have the right to:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 flex flex-col gap-2 mb-3">
          <li>access your data and receive a copy of it;</li>
          <li>have it rectified, erased, or its processing restricted;</li>
          <li>object to processing, and to data portability;</li>
          <li>withdraw your consent at any time where we rely on it, without affecting processing already carried out;</li>
          <li>lodge a complaint with a data protection supervisory authority — in the EU, the authority in your country of residence or work; in Türkiye, the Kişisel Verileri Koruma Kurumu (KVKK).</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          To exercise any of these rights, contact us at
          <a href="mailto:hi@backlex.com" class="text-foreground underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-primary transition-colors">hi@backlex.com</a>.
          We respond within the statutory time limits (30 days under the KVKK; one month under the GDPR).
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-[19px] font-semibold text-foreground -tracking-[0.02em] mb-3">9. Third-Party Services</h2>
        <p>
          The Service may use third-party infrastructure, authentication, and
          payment providers. These providers only access the data needed to
          deliver the Service and are subject to their own privacy obligations.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-[19px] font-semibold text-foreground -tracking-[0.02em] mb-3">10. Changes</h2>
        <p>
          We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. When we make
          material changes we will update the "Last updated" date on this page.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-[19px] font-semibold text-foreground -tracking-[0.02em] mb-3">11. Contact</h2>
        <p>
          For questions about this Privacy Policy or your personal data, contact
          us at
          <a href="mailto:hi@backlex.com" class="text-foreground underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-primary transition-colors">hi@backlex.com</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
